<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tardu Shad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 630</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tardu Shad was a son of Tong Yabghu Qaghan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a>, installed around 625 as yabghu, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a>, the former Hephthalite lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>, with his seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunduz">Kunduz</a>. The Chinese pilgrim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> visited his court around 630, shortly before Tardu was poisoned in a court intrigue.</p></div>
